  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>filloutliers</keyword>
  <short_description>Detect and replace outliers in numeric data.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>B = filloutliers(A, fillmethod)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>B = filloutliers(A, fillmethod, method)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>B = filloutliers(A, fillmethod, 'percentiles', threshold)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>B = filloutliers(A, fillmethod, movmethod, window)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>B = filloutliers(..., dim)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>B = filloutliers(..., Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[B, TF, L, U, C] = filloutliers(...)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>filloutliers</b> detects outliers in a numeric array and replaces them using a selected fill method.</p>
    <p>Fill methods include <b>previous</b>, <b>next</b>, <b>nearest</b>, <b>linear</b>, <b>pchip</b>, <b>clip</b>, or a numeric scalar constant. Detection methods and name-value arguments are shared with <b>isoutlier</b>. The <b>OutlierLocations</b> name-value argument can provide a logical mask directly.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[A = [57 59 60 100 59 58 57 58 300 61 62 60 62 58 57];
B = filloutliers(A, 'linear')]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[A = [60 59 49 49 58 100 61 57 48 58];
[B, TF, L, U, C] = filloutliers(A, 'clip')]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
